      "content": "---\ntitle: Antimony Ingot\nslug: antimony-ingot\ntype: item\nkingdom: Material\nitem_class: Common\ncategory: Ingot\nsubcategory: Metal\nmaterial_type: Metal\nmaterial_form: Ingot\nmaterial_family: Antimony\nsource_items:\n  - Antimony Ore\nweight: 0.8kg\nweight_class: Light\ndurability: Low\nenchantment_affinity: \"12% (+0 dice)\"\nmarket_value: 8 Marks\nimage: Antimony Ingot.png\ntags:\n  - items\n  - materials\n  - metal\n  - ingot\n  - common\nvisibility: public\n---\n\n# Antimony Ingot\n\n## Effect\nAntimony Ingots are brittle but structurally influential, used to reinforce alloys and improve the rigidity of softer metals.\n\n---\n\n## Crafting Use\n- Alloy reinforcement\n- Structural balancing in metal crafting\n- Artificer and alchemical components\n\n---\n\n## Material Traits\n- Brittle and rigid  \n- Not suitable for direct weapon or armor crafting  \n- Improves hardness and form retention in alloys  \n\n---\n\n## Alloy Use\n- [[Pewter Ingot]]\n- Advanced alloy systems (future)\n\n---\n\n## Enchantment Use\n- Enhances durability of enchanted structures  \n- Reduces warping under magical stress  \n\n---\n\n## Crafting Source\n- Requires: 4x [[Antimony Ore]]\n\n---\n\n## Quote\n*\"Strength is not always what stands — but what prevents collapse.\"*\n",
      "body": "# Antimony Ingot\n\n## Effect\nAntimony Ingots are brittle but structurally influential, used to reinforce alloys and improve the rigidity of softer metals.\n\n---\n\n## Crafting Use\n- Alloy reinforcement\n- Structural balancing in metal crafting\n- Artificer and alchemical components\n\n---\n\n## Material Traits\n- Brittle and rigid  \n- Not suitable for direct weapon or armor crafting  \n- Improves hardness and form retention in alloys  \n\n---\n\n## Alloy Use\n- [[Pewter Ingot]]\n- Advanced alloy systems (future)\n\n---\n\n## Enchantment Use\n- Enhances durability of enchanted structures  \n- Reduces warping under magical stress  \n\n---\n\n## Crafting Source\n- Requires: 4x [[Antimony Ore]]\n\n---\n\n## Quote\n*\"Strength is not always what stands — but what prevents collapse.\"*",
