      "sourceFolder": "content/materials/5-epic/metals/arricallium-ingot",
      "content": "---\ntitle: Arricallium Ingot\nslug: arricallium-ingot\ntype: item\nkingdom: Material\nitem_class: Epic\ncategory: Ingot\nsubcategory: Metal\nmaterial_type: Metal\nmaterial_form: Ingot\nmaterial_family: Arricallium\nsource_items:\n  - Arricallium Ore\nweight: 1.6kg\nweight_class: Medium-Light\ndurability: High\nenchantment_affinity: \"80% (+6 dice)\"\ndamage_modifier: +4\narmor_modifier: +3\nmarket_value: 300–450 Marks (Restricted Trade)\ntags:\n  - items\n  - materials\n  - metal\n  - ingot\n  - epic\nvisibility: public\n---\n\n# Arricallium Ingot\n\n## Effect\nArricallium Ingots produce a refined metal that excels at conducting and amplifying magical energy, making it ideal for spellcasting equipment and magical constructs.\n\n---\n\n## Appearance\nArricallium Ingots are smooth, metallic bars with faint glowing veins running beneath the surface. These veins shift slowly, as if energy is continuously flowing through the metal.\n\nThe surface emits a subtle hum when held near magical sources.\n\n---\n\n## Lore\nOnce refined, Arricallium becomes one of the most valuable materials for magical construction. It is widely used in advanced spellcasting tools, arcane conduits, and high-tier enchanted equipment.\n\nDespite its stability, improper handling during forging can result in violent energy discharge.\n\n---\n\n## Material Traits\n- Excellent magical conductivity  \n- Maintains stability under sustained magical use  \n- Lightweight compared to other Epic metals  \n- Sensitive to overload if improperly used  \n\n---\n\n## Enchantment Use\n- Exceptional affinity with **Air** and **Fire**  \n- Enhances:\n  - Spellcasting  \n  - Channeling  \n  - Energy-based enchantments  \n- Poor synergy with purely physical builds  \n\n---\n\n## Combat Integration\n- +4 Damage Modifier  \n- +3 Armor Modifier  \n- Favours caster, hybrid, and magic-focused builds  \n\n---\n\n## Crafting Source\n- Requires 4x [[Arricallium Ore]]  \n- Requires energy-stabilised forge  \n\n---\n\n## Quote\n*\"Power flows through it — not into it.\"*\n",
      "body": "# Arricallium Ingot\n\n## Effect\nArricallium Ingots produce a refined metal that excels at conducting and amplifying magical energy, making it ideal for spellcasting equipment and magical constructs.\n\n---\n\n## Appearance\nArricallium Ingots are smooth, metallic bars with faint glowing veins running beneath the surface. These veins shift slowly, as if energy is continuously flowing through the metal.\n\nThe surface emits a subtle hum when held near magical sources.\n\n---\n\n## Lore\nOnce refined, Arricallium becomes one of the most valuable materials for magical construction. It is widely used in advanced spellcasting tools, arcane conduits, and high-tier enchanted equipment.\n\nDespite its stability, improper handling during forging can result in violent energy discharge.\n\n---\n\n## Material Traits\n- Excellent magical conductivity  \n- Maintains stability under sustained magical use  \n- Lightweight compared to other Epic metals  \n- Sensitive to overload if improperly used  \n\n---\n\n## Enchantment Use\n- Exceptional affinity with **Air** and **Fire**  \n- Enhances:\n  - Spellcasting  \n  - Channeling  \n  - Energy-based enchantments  \n- Poor synergy with purely physical builds  \n\n---\n\n## Combat Integration\n- +4 Damage Modifier  \n- +3 Armor Modifier  \n- Favours caster, hybrid, and magic-focused builds  \n\n---\n\n## Crafting Source\n- Requires 4x [[Arricallium Ore]]  \n- Requires energy-stabilised forge  \n\n---\n\n## Quote\n*\"Power flows through it — not into it.\"*",
