      "content": "---\ntitle: Bismuth Ore\nslug: bismuth-ore\ntype: item\nkingdom: Mineral\nitem_class: Rare\ncategory: Ore\nsubcategory: Metal\nmaterial_type: Metal\nmaterial_form: Ore\nmaterial_family: Bismuth\nsource_items: []\nrefines_into: Bismuth Ingot\nrefinement_ratio: \"4:1\"\nweight_class: Light\ndurability: Low\nenchantment_affinity: \"70% (+5 dice)\"\nmarket_value: 26 Marks\ntags:\n  - items\n  - minerals\n  - metal\n  - ore\n  - rare\nvisibility: public\n---\n\n# Bismuth Ore\n\n## Effect\nBismuth Ore forms in unstable crystalline structures that react unpredictably to magical and environmental input. It carries volatile energy that can either amplify or distort magical effects.\n\n---\n## Appearance\nBismuth Ore forms in jagged, geometric clusters with sharp, stepped edges that resemble fractured crystal structures. Its surface displays shifting iridescent colours — purples, blues, greens, and golds — that change depending on the angle of light.\n\nThe edges of the ore appear unstable, subtly warping or realigning when viewed from different perspectives, as if the structure is never fully fixed.\n\n---\n## Lore\nBismuth is born in places where magic fractures reality — wild magic zones, broken ley lines, and unstable rifts. Its crystalline patterns constantly shift, reflecting a world that refuses to remain still.\n\n---\n\n## Material & Crafting Traits\n- Crystalline metallic structure  \n- Unstable under sustained stress  \n- Difficult to refine without loss  \n- Found in high-risk magical environments  \n\n---\n\n## Refinement\n- Smelts into: [[Bismuth Ingot]]  \n- Ratio: 4 Ore → 1 Ingot  \n- Notes: Refinement may produce unstable or imperfect ingots if not carefully controlled  \n\n---\n\n## Alloy Use\n- Chaos-based alloys (future)\n\n---\n\n## Enchantment Use\n- Very high affinity with volatile and chaotic magic  \n- Amplifies power but reduces stability  \n- Can cause unpredictable magical interactions  \n\n---\n\n## Quote\n*\"It does not obey — it reacts.\"*\n",
      "body": "# Bismuth Ore\n\n## Effect\nBismuth Ore forms in unstable crystalline structures that react unpredictably to magical and environmental input. It carries volatile energy that can either amplify or distort magical effects.\n\n---\n## Appearance\nBismuth Ore forms in jagged, geometric clusters with sharp, stepped edges that resemble fractured crystal structures. Its surface displays shifting iridescent colours — purples, blues, greens, and golds — that change depending on the angle of light.\n\nThe edges of the ore appear unstable, subtly warping or realigning when viewed from different perspectives, as if the structure is never fully fixed.\n\n---\n## Lore\nBismuth is born in places where magic fractures reality — wild magic zones, broken ley lines, and unstable rifts. Its crystalline patterns constantly shift, reflecting a world that refuses to remain still.\n\n---\n\n## Material & Crafting Traits\n- Crystalline metallic structure  \n- Unstable under sustained stress  \n- Difficult to refine without loss  \n- Found in high-risk magical environments  \n\n---\n\n## Refinement\n- Smelts into: [[Bismuth Ingot]]  \n- Ratio: 4 Ore → 1 Ingot  \n- Notes: Refinement may produce unstable or imperfect ingots if not carefully controlled  \n\n---\n\n## Alloy Use\n- Chaos-based alloys (future)\n\n---\n\n## Enchantment Use\n- Very high affinity with volatile and chaotic magic  \n- Amplifies power but reduces stability  \n- Can cause unpredictable magical interactions  \n\n---\n\n## Quote\n*\"It does not obey — it reacts.\"*",
