      "content": "---\ntitle: Duranium Ore\nslug: duranium-ore\ntype: item\nkingdom: Mineral\nitem_class: Epic\ncategory: Ore\nsubcategory: Metal\nmaterial_type: Metal\nmaterial_form: Ore\nmaterial_family: Duranium\nsource_items: []\nrefines_into: Duranium Ingot\nrefinement_ratio: \"4:1\"\nweight_class: Very Heavy\ndurability: Very High\nenchantment_affinity: \"65% (+5 dice)\"\nmarket_value: 250–380 Marks (Restricted Trade)\ntags:\n  - items\n  - minerals\n  - metal\n  - ore\n  - epic\nvisibility: public\n---\n\n# Duranium Ore\n\n## Effect\nDuranium Ore is a dense, energy-reactive metal that forms in regions of extreme pressure and force. It naturally absorbs and stabilises incoming energy, making it highly resilient to both physical and environmental stress.\n\n---\n\n## Appearance\nDuranium Ore appears as a dark grey metallic stone with faint, shifting patterns beneath its surface. These patterns move slowly, like energy being redistributed through the material.\n\nWhen struck, subtle ripples travel across the ore before fading.\n\n---\n\n## Lore\nDuranium forms deep beneath the surface of the world or within areas of intense energy convergence. These environments compress and fuse energy into physical form, creating a metal that responds to force rather than resisting it.\n\nIt is rare and difficult to extract due to its density and reactive nature.\n\n---\n\n## Material Traits\n- Extremely dense and heavy  \n- Absorbs and redistributes energy  \n- Stable under high pressure and force  \n- Difficult to mine and transport  \n\n---\n\n## Refinement\n- Smelts into: [[Duranium Ingot]]  \n- Ratio: 4 Ore → 1 Ingot  \n- Requires high-energy or pressure-stable forge  \n\n---\n\n## Enchantment Use\n- Moderate affinity with **Earth** and **Air**  \n- Enhances:\n  - Stability  \n  - Defensive effects  \n  - Energy control  \n\n---\n\n## Quote\n*\"It does not break — it changes how the world strikes it.\"*\n",
      "body": "# Duranium Ore\n\n## Effect\nDuranium Ore is a dense, energy-reactive metal that forms in regions of extreme pressure and force. It naturally absorbs and stabilises incoming energy, making it highly resilient to both physical and environmental stress.\n\n---\n\n## Appearance\nDuranium Ore appears as a dark grey metallic stone with faint, shifting patterns beneath its surface. These patterns move slowly, like energy being redistributed through the material.\n\nWhen struck, subtle ripples travel across the ore before fading.\n\n---\n\n## Lore\nDuranium forms deep beneath the surface of the world or within areas of intense energy convergence. These environments compress and fuse energy into physical form, creating a metal that responds to force rather than resisting it.\n\nIt is rare and difficult to extract due to its density and reactive nature.\n\n---\n\n## Material Traits\n- Extremely dense and heavy  \n- Absorbs and redistributes energy  \n- Stable under high pressure and force  \n- Difficult to mine and transport  \n\n---\n\n## Refinement\n- Smelts into: [[Duranium Ingot]]  \n- Ratio: 4 Ore → 1 Ingot  \n- Requires high-energy or pressure-stable forge  \n\n---\n\n## Enchantment Use\n- Moderate affinity with **Earth** and **Air**  \n- Enhances:\n  - Stability  \n  - Defensive effects  \n  - Energy control  \n\n---\n\n## Quote\n*\"It does not break — it changes how the world strikes it.\"*",
