      "content": "---\ntitle: Necronium Ore\nslug: necronium-ore\ntype: item\nkingdom: Mineral\nitem_class: Mythic\ncategory: Ore\nsubcategory: Metal\nmaterial_type: Metal\nmaterial_form: Ore\nmaterial_family: Necronium\nsource_items: []\nrefines_into: Necronium Ingot\nrefinement_ratio: \"4:1\"\nformation_type: Event / Death Saturation\nweight_class: Medium\ndurability: Very High\nenchantment_affinity: \"75% (+6 dice)\"\nmarket_value: 280–420 Marks (Restricted Trade)\ntags:\n  - items\n  - minerals\n  - metal\n  - ore\n  - mythic\nvisibility: public\n---\n\n# Necronium Ore\n\n## Effect\nNecronium Ore is a condensed form of death energy that reacts to living presence. It slowly drains vitality from nearby living creatures, converting it into dormant necrotic energy within the material.\n\n---\n\n## Appearance\nNecronium Ore appears as dark, ash-grey stone with faint violet undertones. Its surface seems unnaturally still, with subtle drifting patterns beneath it like slow-moving smoke.\n\nIn proximity to living beings, the surrounding air feels colder and quieter.\n\n---\n\n## Lore\nNecronium Ore does not form through traditional geological processes. Instead, it manifests in locations where death energy has accumulated over time — battlefields, mass graves, and necrotic domains.\n\nThese formations are rare and unstable, often appearing after significant events rather than through natural mining veins.\n\n---\n\n## Material Traits\n- Forms from death saturation rather than mining  \n- Reacts to nearby life energy  \n- Stable under necrotic influence  \n- Weak under strong Light-aligned environments  \n\n---\n\n## Refinement\n- Smelts into: [[Necronium Ingot]]  \n- Ratio: 4 Ore → 1 Ingot  \n- Requires necrotic-aligned forge or controlled environment  \n\n---\n\n## Enchantment Use\n- Strong affinity with **Death**  \n- Enhances:\n  - Decay effects  \n  - Life-drain  \n  - Curse-based enchantments  \n\n---\n\n## Quote\n*\"It forms where life ends — and lingers where it should not.\"*\n",
