      "sourcePath": "content/minerals/4-rare/ores/pure-silver-ore/index.md",
      "sourceFolder": "content/minerals/4-rare/ores/pure-silver-ore",
      "content": "---\ntitle: Pure Silver Ore\nslug: pure-silver-ore\ntype: item\nkingdom: Mineral\nitem_class: Rare\ncategory: Ore\nsubcategory: Metal\nmaterial_type: Metal\nmaterial_form: Ore\nmaterial_family: Pure Silver\nsource_items: []\nrefines_into: Pure Silver Ingot\nrefinement_ratio: \"4:1\"\nweight_class: Light\ndurability: Moderate\nenchantment_affinity: \"60% (+4 dice)\"\nmarket_value: 22 Marks\ntags:\n  - items\n  - minerals\n  - metal\n  - ore\n  - rare\nvisibility: public\n---\n\n# Pure Silver Ore\n\n## Effect\nPure Silver Ore is infused with the essence of **Light itself** — not life, but clarity, purity, and illumination. It emits a faint glow and disrupts shadow and corruption.\n\n---\n## Appearance\nPure Silver Ore appears as bright, pale metal veins running through stone, noticeably cleaner and more luminous than common silver. Its surface reflects light with a soft, steady glow, giving it an almost pristine, untouched quality.\n\nEven in low light, the ore maintains a faint brightness, as though holding onto light rather than reflecting it.\n\n---\n## Lore\nUnlike common silver, Pure Silver is not simply refined — it is *formed*. Where Light condenses into the physical world, veins of Pure Silver emerge, untouched by impurity. It is said to be the metal that Light chose to inhabit.\n\n---\n\n## Material & Crafting Traits\n- Emits a faint glow in darkness  \n- Naturally repels corruption and shadow  \n- Sensitive to impurity during refinement  \n- Requires precise heat control to maintain purity  \n\n---\n\n## Refinement\n- Smelts into: [[Pure Silver Ingot]]  \n- Ratio: 4 Ore → 1 Ingot  \n- Notes: Overheating reduces purity and effectiveness  \n\n---\n\n## Alloy Use\n- Light-aligned alloys (future)\n\n---\n\n## Enchantment Use\n- High affinity with **Light** magic  \n- Enhances purification and illumination effects  \n- Reduces effectiveness of Dark-aligned enchantments  \n\n---\n\n## Quote\n*\"It does not shine — it reveals.\"*\n",
