      "content": "---\ntitle: Tin Ore\nslug: tin-ore\ntype: item\nkingdom: Mineral\nitem_class: Common\ncategory: Ore\nsubcategory: Metal\nmaterial_type: Metal\nmaterial_form: Ore\nmaterial_family: Tin\nsource_items: []\nrefines_into: Tin Ingot\nrefinement_ratio: \"4:1\"\nweight_class: Light\ndurability: Low\nenchantment_affinity: \"10% (+0 dice)\"\nmarket_value: 1 Marks\ntags:\n  - items\n  - minerals\n  - metal\n  - ore\n  - common\nvisibility: public\n---\n\n# Tin Ore\n\n## Effect\nTin Ore is a soft, low-density material with minimal standalone use, but it plays a crucial role in stabilising alloys and enabling stronger metal compositions.\n\n---\n\n## Lore\nCalled the *“Silent Catalyst,”* tin lacks strength but enables greatness in others. Entire ages of advancement depended on its quiet presence in alloy crafting.\n\n---\n\n## Material & Crafting Traits\n- Very soft and easy to refine  \n- High impurity loss during smelting  \n- Essential for alloy creation  \n- Common training material  \n\n---\n\n## Refinement\n- Smelts into: [[Tin Ingot]]\n- Ratio: 4 Ore → 1 Ingot\n- Notes: High loss due to impurities\n\n---\n\n## Alloy Use\n- [[Bronze Ingot]]\n\n---\n\n## Enchantment Use\n- Minimal direct use  \n- Stabilises enchantments in alloys  \n\n---\n\n## Quote\n*\"It does not shine — but it makes others stronger.\"*\n",
      "body": "# Tin Ore\n\n## Effect\nTin Ore is a soft, low-density material with minimal standalone use, but it plays a crucial role in stabilising alloys and enabling stronger metal compositions.\n\n---\n\n## Lore\nCalled the *“Silent Catalyst,”* tin lacks strength but enables greatness in others. Entire ages of advancement depended on its quiet presence in alloy crafting.\n\n---\n\n## Material & Crafting Traits\n- Very soft and easy to refine  \n- High impurity loss during smelting  \n- Essential for alloy creation  \n- Common training material  \n\n---\n\n## Refinement\n- Smelts into: [[Tin Ingot]]\n- Ratio: 4 Ore → 1 Ingot\n- Notes: High loss due to impurities\n\n---\n\n## Alloy Use\n- [[Bronze Ingot]]\n\n---\n\n## Enchantment Use\n- Minimal direct use  \n- Stabilises enchantments in alloys  \n\n---\n\n## Quote\n*\"It does not shine — but it makes others stronger.\"*",
