      "sourcePath": "content/minerals/7-legendary/ores/vibranium-ore/index.md",
      "sourceFolder": "content/minerals/7-legendary/ores/vibranium-ore",
      "content": "---\ntitle: Vibranium Ore\nslug: vibranium-ore\ntype: item\nkingdom: Mineral\nitem_class: Legendary\ncategory: Ore\nsubcategory: Metal\nmaterial_type: Metal\nmaterial_form: Ore\nmaterial_family: Vibranium\nsource_items: []\nrefines_into: Vibranium Ingot\nrefinement_ratio: \"4:1\"\nformation_type: Resonant Celestial Impact\nweight_class: Medium\ndurability: Extremely High\nenchantment_affinity: \"75% (+6 dice)\"\nmarket_value: 300–480 Marks (Legendary Trade)\ntags:\n  - items\n  - minerals\n  - metal\n  - ore\n  - legendary\nvisibility: public\n---\n\n# Vibranium Ore\n\n## Effect\nVibranium Ore is a rare resonant metal capable of absorbing, storing, and redistributing kinetic force through internal harmonic vibrations.\n\nThe ore naturally reacts to movement, impact, and sound, creating subtle resonance pulses throughout its structure.\n\n---\n\n## Appearance\nVibranium Ore appears as dark silver stone threaded with faint blue-white resonance lines that pulse softly under movement or sound.\n\nWhen struck, the ore emits a low harmonic tone that lingers briefly in the air.\n\n---\n\n## Lore\nAncient records claim Vibranium first formed after a celestial impact fused cosmic energy with the raw motion of the world itself.\n\nUnlike most metals, Vibranium does not simply endure force — it learns from it, storing kinetic resonance within its structure and releasing it gradually over time.\n\nBecause of this property, the metal became highly prized among artificers, engineers, and advanced forge guilds.\n\n---\n\n## Material Traits\n- Absorbs and redistributes kinetic force  \n- Resonates with movement and vibration  \n- Extremely resistant to shattering  \n- Requires harmonic refinement techniques  \n\n---\n\n## Refinement\n- Smelts into: [[Vibranium Ingot]]  \n- Ratio: 4 Ore → 1 Ingot  \n- Requires harmonic forge or resonance-controlled refinement  \n\n---\n\n## Enchantment Use\n- Strong affinity with **Air**  \n- Enhances:\n  - Resonance enchantments  \n  - Movement-based abilities  \n  - Kinetic manipulation effects  \n\n---\n\n## Quote\n*\"The metal remembers every strike.\"*\n",
      "body": "# Vibranium Ore\n\n## Effect\nVibranium Ore is a rare resonant metal capable of absorbing, storing, and redistributing kinetic force through internal harmonic vibrations.\n\nThe ore naturally reacts to movement, impact, and sound, creating subtle resonance pulses throughout its structure.\n\n---\n\n## Appearance\nVibranium Ore appears as dark silver stone threaded with faint blue-white resonance lines that pulse softly under movement or sound.\n\nWhen struck, the ore emits a low harmonic tone that lingers briefly in the air.\n\n---\n\n## Lore\nAncient records claim Vibranium first formed after a celestial impact fused cosmic energy with the raw motion of the world itself.\n\nUnlike most metals, Vibranium does not simply endure force — it learns from it, storing kinetic resonance within its structure and releasing it gradually over time.\n\nBecause of this property, the metal became highly prized among artificers, engineers, and advanced forge guilds.\n\n---\n\n## Material Traits\n- Absorbs and redistributes kinetic force  \n- Resonates with movement and vibration  \n- Extremely resistant to shattering  \n- Requires harmonic refinement techniques  \n\n---\n\n## Refinement\n- Smelts into: [[Vibranium Ingot]]  \n- Ratio: 4 Ore → 1 Ingot  \n- Requires harmonic forge or resonance-controlled refinement  \n\n---\n\n## Enchantment Use\n- Strong affinity with **Air**  \n- Enhances:\n  - Resonance enchantments  \n  - Movement-based abilities  \n  - Kinetic manipulation effects  \n\n---\n\n## Quote\n*\"The metal remembers every strike.\"*",
