      "searchTerms": "cavern sprite race  {\"title\":\"cavern sprite\",\"slug\":\"cavern-sprite\",\"type\":\"race\",\"racecategory\":\"small races\",\"secondarycategory\":\"sprite races\",\"tertiarycategory\":\"\",\"playable\":true,\"size\":\"\",\"movement\":\"8m (walking)\",\"languages\":[\"sprite - common\"],\"magicaffinity\":[\"dark magic - earth magic\"],\"essenceaffinity\":[],\"tags\":[\"race\",\"small-races\",\"sprite-races\"],\"images\":\"\",\"male\":\"assets/races/cavern-sprite/cavern-sprite-male-adult.png\",\"female\":\"assets/races/cavern-sprite/cavern-sprite-female-adult.png\",\"visibility\":\"public\",\"sourceorder\":27} # cavern sprite\n\n## overview\n**race name:** cavern sprite  \n**race category:** small races\n**race type:** sprite  \n**size:** small\n**average height:** 85–130 cm\n**average weight:** 18–55 kg  \n**lifespan:** 180–260 years  \n**home region:** deep caverns, crystal hollows, fungal depths, underground ruins  \n**primary language:** sprite speak \n**secondary languages:** common, undercommon\n**rarity:** rare  \n**alignment tendencies:** neutral good, true neutral, chaotic neutral\n\n# cavern sprite — short summary paragraph\n\n> cavern sprites are small subterranean feykin who dwell deep beneath the world within crystal caverns, fungal forests, and forgotten underground ruins. known for their gray-toned skin, sharp elven features, and silent movements, they are masters of stealth, resonance, and survival within the endless dark. curious yet cautious, cavern sprites preserve the balance of underground ecosystems and rarely trust surface dwellers.\n\n# official cavern sprite motto\n\n> **“stone, shadow, silence.”**\n\n![[pasted image 20260525214029.png]]\n\n## racial features\n- height range:\n  - 50 cm to 100 cm  \n\n- weight range:\n  - 10 kg to 25 kg  \n\n- skin:\n  - thin, smooth skin adapted to low light  \n  - colour range:\n    - pale grey → charcoal → deep black  \n\n- hair:\n  - fine and soft, often uneven or naturally layered  \n  - colour range:\n    - brown → ash → pale blonde  \n\n- eyes:\n  - large, slanted, highly sensitive to light  \n  - colour range:\n    - grey → dark brown → near-black  \n  - reflect light faintly in darkness  \n\n- hands:\n  - small, nimble fingers  \n  - excellent grip for climbing and navigating tight spaces  \n\n- face:\n  - narrow features with sharp cheekbones  \n  - expressions subtle and difficult to read  \n\n- ears:\n  - small with slight pointed tips  \n  - highly sensitive to sound vibrations  \n\n- markings:\n  - faint dark patches or mineral-like streaks in skin  \n  - some may have subtle glowing veins in deep darkness  \n\n- body:\n  - small, lightweight build  \n  - movement is quick, quiet, and precise  \n\n---\n\n## racial characteristics\n| characteristic | buff/debuff | stat rolls | characteristic tier cap |\n| -------------- | ----------- | ---------- | :---------------------: |\n| strength       | -4          | 3d6        |         tier 2          |\n| dexterity      | +1          | 4d6        |         tier 5          |\n| agility        | +2          | 4d6        |         tier 5          |\n| constitution   | -1          | 3d6        |         tier 3          |\n| endurance      | 0           | 3d6        |         tier 4          |\n| intelligence   | 0           | 4d6        |         tier 4          |\n| wisdom         | +1          | 4d6        |         tier 5          |\n| charisma       | 0           | 4d6        |         tier 5          |\n| luck           | 0           | 3d6        |         tier 5          |\n\n---\n\n## racial traits\n### racial bond – split soul\nsprite are born with **half a soul**.\n\n- the other half manifests as a **pixie**\n- pixie and sprite can sense one another across great distances\n- when within close proximity, magic flows more smoothly\n\nif the bond is damaged or severed, the pixie and/or sprite becomes **unstable**, suffering narrative and mechanical consequences.\n\n### dark vision\n- can see clearly in darkness up to 30m  \n- no penalties in low-light environments  \n\n### light footing\n- ignore movement penalties in:\n  - loose stone  \n  - uneven cave terrain  \n- reduced noise when moving over rock/stone\n\n### cavern adaptation\n- advantage on checks related to:\n  - navigating caves  \n  - detecting structural instability  \n  - finding hidden paths  \n\n### shadow affinity\n- increased effectiveness when:\n  - in darkness  \n  - out of direct light  \n\n### imbued strike (adapted)\n- can infuse attacks or actions with dark/earth energy  \n- adds minor magical effect (scales later with system)\n\n---\n\n## lore\ninformation coming soon.\n\n## culture\ninformation coming soon.\n\n## historical figures\ninformation coming soon.\n\n## settlements\ninformation coming soon.\n\n## relations\ninformation coming soon.\n\n## traits & biology\n- small size allows movement through tight spaces  \n- can climb rocky surfaces with reduced difficulty  \n- gains stealth advantage in darkness  \n\n---\n\n### ⚠️ drawbacks\n- very low physical strength  \n- fragile compared to larger races  \n- sensitive to bright light (possible disadvantage in strong light)\n\n## gallery\ninformation coming soon.\n\n## gm notes\ngm-only information coming soon."
